  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows negative bias (e.g., -0.25 or below) to counteract overconfidence in upward moves.",
    "Reduce forecast magnitude by 5-10% when true outcomes consistently lag behind model predictions (e.g., 3-5 day delays in price recovery).",
    "Apply a downward correction of 3-8% after sharp spikes in model forecasts, especially if sentiment is neutral or slightly positive, to prevent overshoot.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent true outcomes when sentiment is positive (e.g., >0.50), to avoid mean reversion misses.",
    "When sentiment is neutral (0.00) and history shows persistent underperformance, apply a 2-5% upward bias to compensate for lagged mean reversion.",
    "For long-term (30-day) forecasts, reduce volatility in predictions when sentiment is stable (no recent changes), to avoid overfitting to short-term noise."
  ]
}
